From 50050ed6524be124e902fa0217dd13ca34650e90 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 05:59:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix retire dialog being stuck when a popup appears over it

The prestige modal overlay (z-index 400) sat above every app popup, but App
marks the page inert while a popup is showing, so the dialog hid the popup and
could not be clicked itself. Lower it to 90 so popups render on top.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0115oetuNdXfmPV3rBHJ3PDF
---
 hyperloop-ui/src/pages/PrestigePage.css | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/hyperloop-ui/src/pages/PrestigePage.css b/hyperloop-ui/src/pages/PrestigePage.css
index c26ce5d..ce84b6c 100644
--- a/hyperloop-ui/src/pages/PrestigePage.css
+++ b/hyperloop-ui/src/pages/PrestigePage.css
@@ -645,7 +645,11 @@
 .prestige-modal-overlay {
     position: fixed;
     inset: 0;
-    z-index: 400;
+    /* Must stay BELOW every app-level popup (the lowest are the rank-up, reveal and shop overlays at 100). This overlay
+       lives inside the page, and App makes the page `inert` while a popup is showing: at 400 the "Retire this terminal?"
+       dialog covered the popup, hiding it, while being inert itself - so neither could be clicked and the dialog
+       couldn't be closed. Below the popups, the popup shows on top and the dialog is usable again once it's dismissed. */
+    z-index: 90;
     background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.7);
     display: flex;
     align-items: center;
-- 
